    "created_at": "2023-09-01T10:45:33Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-09-01T10:57:40Z",
    "body": "Perhaps it's reasonable for Starship to attempt a `--short-version` and otherwise return nil?\r\n\r\nThat would mean Elixir <= 1.2 would lose their version display (but the icon can still be visible), but considering the slow down caused by starting the beam that may be acceptable. \r\n\r\nFor comparison on my system:\r\n\r\n```\r\n➜ time elixir --short-version\r\n1.15.4\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________\r\nExecuted in    1.72 millis    fish           external\r\n   usr time    1.68 millis  195.00 micros    1.49 millis\r\n   sys time    0.09 millis   87.00 micros    0.00 millis\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n➜ time elixir --version\r\nErlang/OTP 26 [erts-14.0.2] [source] [64-bit] [smp:8:8] [ds:8:8:10] [async-threads:1] [jit:ns]\r\n\r\nElixir 1.15.4 (compiled with Erlang/OTP 26)\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________\r\nExecuted in  345.59 millis    fish           external\r\n   usr time  870.15 millis  260.00 micros  869.89 millis\r\n   sys time  147.06 millis  117.00 micros  146.94 millis\r\n\r\n\r\n```",
    "author_association": "NONE",
